Changes made by JavCMS to third-party files
-------------------------------------------

The Apache License 2.0 and the LGPL ask that changed files say that they were
changed. JavCMS files with a JavCMS notice say so at the top. Third-party files
carry no JavCMS notice (JavCMS adds nothing to them), so their changes are
listed in NOTICE.CHANGED-FILES.txt, which comes with every copy and is the
change notice for those files. That file is generated for each release. It names every file of the MacCMS
v2023.1000.3051 release (which also ships ThinkPHP 5.0.24, the vendor/
packages and the bundled static libraries) and of the libraries that JavCMS
bundles in addition (TinyMCE 5.4.0, KindEditor 4.1.12, CKEditor 4.11.1,
UMeditor 1.2.2, CodeMirror 5.42.2, Layui 2.9.13 and 2.7.6) that is different
in this package from its original release, with the kind of change (code,
messages, comments, formatting, content or configuration), who made it
(changes that were already in the copy JavCMS received from ApiiCMS are
marked "as received (ApiiCMS)") and its date.

- PclZip 2.8.2 (application/common/util/PclZip.php, LGPL-2.1) was changed by
  JavCMS in 2026: a PHP 8 constructor was added, error messages were reworded
  and comments were rewritten in plain English.
- PHP QR Code 1.1.4 (application/common/util/Qrcode.php, LGPL-3.0) was changed
  by JavCMS in 2026: error messages were reworded and comments were rewritten
  in plain English.
  The date of the last change of both files is in NOTICE.CHANGED-FILES.txt.
  Their copyright and license notices are kept as their authors published them.
- TinyMCE 5.4.0 (static/editor/tinymce/, LGPL-2.1) and KindEditor 4.1.12
  (static/editor/kindeditor/, LGPL-2.1) came to JavCMS through ApiiCMS, which
  had added the TinyMCE language files langs/vi-vn.js and langs/zh_CN.js and
  changed kindeditor-all-min.js (2024). JavCMS changed them in 2026: some error
